110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (Currently, Shoelotskey operates using traditional, manual logbooks to track customer orders and shoe conditions. This manual approach is prone to human error, data loss, and slow retrieval of information. Furthermore, the business lacks a method for estimating service completion dates, often relying on mental guesswork that lead to missed deadlines or customer frustration. Finally, the absence of a centralized data system prevents the owner from seeing the big picture, making it difficult to identify which services are most profitable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
